  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Four VIPs $V_1$, $V_2$, $V_3$ and $V_4$ are seated on a circular table with 8 other people. How many seating arrangements are there if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q18-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the VIPs are equally spaced around the table.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3!\\times 8! = 241\\,920$\n\nFix $V_1$, arrange the other VIPs in the three equally spaced VIP seats, then arrange the eight other people.",
          "worked": "Fix $V_1$. With 12 people, consecutive VIP positions are three seats apart. The other three VIPs have $3!$ orders in their positions, and the eight other people have $8!$ orders.\n$$N = 3!\\times 8! = 241\\,920.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q18-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the VIPs appear in that clockwise order, not necessarily consecutively.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{11!}{3!} = 6\\,652\\,800$\n\nFix $V_1$; exactly one of the $3!$ clockwise orders of the remaining VIPs is permitted.",
          "worked": "Fix $V_1$. There are $11!$ arrangements of the other people. For any chosen positions of $V_2$, $V_3$ and $V_4$, their $3!$ orders are equally possible, and exactly one gives the required clockwise order.\n$$N = \\frac{11!}{3!} = 6\\,652\\,800.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q18-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the VIPs appear consecutively in that clockwise order.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$8! = 40\\,320$\n\nTreat the four VIPs as one block with a fixed internal order.",
          "worked": "Treat $V_1,V_2,V_3,V_4$ as one block in the specified clockwise order. The block and the eight other people form nine entities around the circle.\n$$N = (9-1)! = 8! = 40\\,320.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
